{"name":"Spinning Wheel","hex":"#f6edda","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinning wheel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domestic device for making yarn or thread; having a single spindle and a wheel driven by hand or foot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinning_wheel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinning wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A spinning wheel is a device for spinning thread or yarn from fibres. It was fundamental to the textile industry prior to the Industrial Revolution. It laid the foundations for later machinery such as the spinning jenny and spinning frame, which displaced the spinning wheel during the Industrial Revolution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Elderlyspinnera.jpg/330px-Elderlyspinnera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinning_wheel","wikidata":"Q58966"},{"title":"Spinning (textiles)","blocks":[{"text":"Spinning is a twisting technique to form yarn from fibers. The fiber intended is drawn out, twisted, and wound onto a bobbin. A few popular fibers that are spun into yarn other than cotton, which is the most popular, are viscose, animal fibers such as wool, and synthetic polyester. Originally done by hand using a spindle whorl, starting in the 500s AD the spinning wheel became the predominant spinning tool across Asia and Europe. The spinning jenny and spinning mule, invented in the late 1700s, made mechanical spinning far more efficient than spinning by hand, and especially made cotton manufacturing one of the most important industries of the Industrial Revolution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Spinning_and_carding_wool_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_XXIX%2C_opposite_69_-_BL.jpg/330px-Spinning_and_carding_wool_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_XXIX%2C_opposite_69_-_BL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinning_(textiles)","wikidata":"Q59172"},{"title":"Spinning Wheel (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Spinning Wheel\" is a song recorded in 1968 by jazz fusion/rock band Blood, Sweat & Tears; it was written by Canadian lead vocalist David Clayton-Thomas and included on its eponymous album, which was released in 1968."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Spinning_Wheel_-_Blood%2C_Sweat_%26_Tears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinning_Wheel_(song)","wikidata":"Q3493521"},{"title":"Wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A wheel is a rotating component intended to turn on an axle bearing. The wheel is one of the key components of the wheel and axle, which is one of the six simple machines. Wheels, in conjunction with axles, allow heavy objects to be moved easily, facilitating transportation, supporting loads, and performing work in machines. Wheels are also used for other purposes, such as a ship's wheel, steering wheel, potter's wheel, and flywheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg/330px-Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel","wikidata":"Q446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hindoo_Spinning-Wheel_%28September_1852%2C_p.108%2C_IX%29_-_Copy.jpg/500px-Hindoo_Spinning-Wheel_%28September_1852%2C_p.108%2C_IX%29_-_Copy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hindoo_Spinning-Wheel_%28September_1852%2C_p.108%2C_IX%29_-_Copy.jpg/500px-Hindoo_Spinning-Wheel_%28September_1852%2C_p.108%2C_IX%29_-_Copy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","al